"answer": "Yes, painless lumps in the neck and drenching night sweats can be signs of Hodgkin lymphoma. According to the provided text, symptoms of Hodgkin lymphoma include painless, swollen lymph nodes in the neck and drenching night sweats [MLP-1262]. Regarding the second question, the most common medical condition leading to an excess buildup of fluid around the lungs (pleural effusion) is congestive heart failure [MLP-4627]."
